# M10. A stiff elbow that still moves, but at about 5°/s, can't reach the pose in time. It isn't stalled (it
# moves faster than 3°/s) and its goal waits within 5° of it (no divergence), so the move's deadline ends it:
# stop, hold and latch motion_timeout. (A blocked elbow is the stall rule, M25.)
expect motion mode ready
key torque-on-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque left on
key slow-left
key pose-ready-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion command arm.go_to_pose started operator_cli
absent 2000 motion fault feedback_divergence
expect 3000 motion fault motion_timeout arm_left
expect motion command arm.go_to_pose faulted operator_cli
key q
